-- `fn` is reserved (marks function-typed parameters in declarations) and
-- cannot be used as a local binding name. The parser rejects `fn=...` at
-- the declaration site with ILO-P011 + a rename-shaped hint, so the agent
-- doesn't waste a retry pattern-matching on the wrong fix.
--
-- WOULD ERROR — `fn` used as a binding name:
--   main>n;fn=5;fn
--   -- ERROR ILO-P011: `fn` is a reserved word and cannot be used as an identifier
--   -- hint: `fn` is reserved (it marks function-typed parameters in
--   --       declarations); rename the binding to e.g. `fv`, `func`, or
--   --       `callback`
--
-- The hint deliberately does NOT restate `use name=expr for bindings`
-- (ml-engineer rerun8 #fn-hint): the user already wrote `name=expr` shape,
-- so the actionable fix is picking a different identifier.
--
-- This example uses `fv` as the rename - 2-char ident, not reserved.

main>n
  fv=5
  fv

-- run: main
-- out: 5
